  "body": "Follow-up to https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/636 and discussion in https://github.com/validator/validator/issues/238\n\nWhile having strict authoring requirements and forgiving processing often serves as an extensibility point, in the case of `<time>` the mismatch does not look particularly meaningful. Alternatives:\n1. Change processing such that having child elements (but presumably not child comments or multiple child text nodes) is a failure, as suggested by @sideshowbarker in https://github.com/validator/validator/issues/238#issuecomment-181226538\n2. Drop the \"A `time` element that does not have a `datetime` content attribute must not have any element descendants\" authoring requirement.\n",
